WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.180
A poster.

2
00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.920
A grey photo on the left, a
block of words on the right.

3
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.340
Slide the photo across to the right.

4
00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.560
Same photo.

5
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:09.890
Same words.

6
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.760
Each time, the eye travels a
different path across the page.

7
00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.370
Nothing new was added.

8
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.740
So why does the poster seem
to say something different?

9
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:23.240
In this mission, you'll see how a
multimodal text makes meaning from words,

10
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:24.980
images and layout.

11
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.620
You'll learn about reading
path, and salience:

12
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.450
what the eye meets first.

13
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.410
And you'll look inside
the image: shot distance,

14
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.310
angle and gaze.

15
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.730
Your mission: explain
why the meaning changes.
